      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In the title compound, C29H25FN2O4, the mean planes of the two indole ring systems (r.m.s. deviations = 0.1392 and 0.0115\u2005Å) are approximately perpendicular to one another, subtending a dihedral angle of 86.0\u2005(5)°; the benzene ring is twisted with respect to the mean planes of the two indole ring systems by 83.3\u2005(2) and 88.1\u2005(4)°, respectively. In the crystal, pairs of N-H⋯O hydrogen bonds link the mol-ecules into centrosymmetric dimers, which are further linked by N-H⋯O hydrogen bonds into supra-molecular chains propagating along the [101] direction."},
